--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this licence does not cover
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence above covers the code written by the Khet Sathi team in this
repository. It does not cover third-party data, values and texts that the
repository contains or that its exports are derived from. Those keep their own
terms; records/credits.txt lists each source and how to cite it. In particular:

- config/dhm_normals_1991_2020.csv: climate normals (c) Department of Hydrology
  and Meteorology (DHM), Government of Nepal, reproduced with attribution for
  validation. DHM states no open licence.
- config/dhm_onset_dates.csv: monsoon onset dates (c) Department of Hydrology
  and Meteorology (DHM), Government of Nepal, reproduced with attribution; the
  site's "has the monsoon shifted?" answer and usual start window come from
  them. DHM states no open licence.
- The Kathmandu Airport station values behind the temperature correction (NOAA
  GHCN-Daily, derived from NOAA's Global Summary of the Day). For data from
  outside the United States the GSOD terms follow WMO Resolution 40: "the data
  or any derived product shall not be provided to other users or be used for
  the re-export of commercial services". The repository holds no station file;
  the exports in site/data/ carry a correction fitted to that station.
- Quotations from FAO, CGIAR-centre and NARC publications in pipeline/words/
  (each with its source) and crop values taken from FAO publications in
  config/crops.json: (c) their publishers. FAO material is commonly licensed
  CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO.
- The files in site/data/ are derived from NASA data, ISRIC SoilGrids
  (CC BY 4.0), ESA WorldCover (CC BY 4.0) and the sources above. Use them with
  the attributions in records/credits.txt.
